{"from": "text:mishnah-negaim-3-1", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:lk-17-14-show-priests", "grade": "B", "note": "Mishnah Nega'im 3:1: 'only a priest may declare them unclean or clean' - the priest's role in the leprosy inspection; redacted c. 200 CE, so it may not describe the practice of the 30s CE exactly. Regraded C to B per the architect's Mishnah ruling (2026-11-15): the Mishnah names the same practice the claim states."}
{"from": "text:mishnah-negaim-3-1", "type": "documented_by", "to": "source:sefaria-negaim-3-1"}
{"from": "text:josephus-ant-1-sodom", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:mt-10-15-sodom-gomorrah-judgment", "grade": "C", "note": "Josephus retells the destruction as history: God 'set it on fire, with its inhabitants' - Sodom remembered as judged in the first century; a reception tradition."}
{"from": "text:josephus-ant-1-sodom", "type": "attests", "to": "person:lot", "grade": "D", "note": "Josephus names Lot in the Sodom retelling - reception of Genesis, not an independent witness to the person."}
{"from": "text:josephus-ant-1-sodom", "type": "attests", "to": "person:lots-wife", "grade": "D", "note": "Josephus says Lot's wife 'was changed into a pillar of salt; for I have seen it, and it remains at this day' - a pilgrimage tradition he reports; reception, not independent evidence."}
{"from": "text:josephus-ant-1-flood", "type": "documented_by", "to": "source:wikisource-ant1-flood-writers"}
